# Agent packs — world model then specialists

Loop: **scan → compressed world model → specialist coding packs**.

Before coding, fetch packs yourself (do not ask for a paste).

**Fastest path — one call:** `GET http://192.168.1.198:8765/audit/packs/bundle?repo=<name>[&token_budget=2500&q=<kw>&limit_specialists=5]`
(world model + ranked specialists + token-capped `briefs_markdown`). CLI: `ai-audit packs --bundle --repo <name>`.
Then claim → fix → close: `POST /audit/packs/{id}/status {"status":"claimed"}` → patch →
`POST /audit/validate_patch {..., "pack_id": "<id>"}` (passing run marks it `resolved`).

Manual path:

1. World model: `GET http://192.168.1.198:8765/audit/packs?kind=world_model`
   - Load `pack-world-ecosystem` plus `pack-world-<repo>` for repos in scope
   - Load `pack-world-architecture-memory` when changing cross-repo boundaries
2. Specialist: `GET /audit/packs?layer=specialist&repo=<name>&q=<keyword>`
   - Then `GET /audit/packs/{id}` or `/brief`

CLI: `ai-audit packs --kind world_model` · `ai-audit packs --layer specialist --repo …`

Constraints from world-model packs win over guesswork (cortex ownership, agent-composer RAG, voluptas ComfyUI, scan `dev`). Verify with pack commands or `POST /audit/validate_patch`.
